      "In a powerful example of Dubai Police’s commitment to investing in people and celebrating inspiring success stories, His Excellency Lieutenant General Abdulla Khalifa Al Marri, the Commander-in-chief of Dubai Police, has honoured Lieutenant Doha Ahmad Muhammad as part of ‘The Group’ initiative, which highlights outstanding and motivating role models within the force.",
      "Lieutenant Doha was recognised for her professional excellence and exceptional personal journey, which reflects the values of resilience, determination, and leadership upheld by Dubai Police. The honour underlines how challenges can be transformed into motivation for achievement and leadership.",
      "Al Marri praised the achievements Lieutenant Doha has accomplished in a relatively short period, noting that they reflect the supportive institutional environment provided by Dubai Police to empower female talent, develop their skills, and offer equal opportunities across all fields, including military training. He emphasised that she represents an inspiring example of the ambitious Emirati woman who is capable of leadership and meaningful contribution.",
      "A Journey Shaped by Resilience",
      "Lieutenant Doha grew up as an orphan, raised with her sisters in an environment of care and support. Despite the hardship of losing her parents, she refused to be defined by circumstances and chose a path of excellence through education, hard work, and self belief.",
      "After becoming a mother to her son Younes, she faced another profound loss when her husband passed away in a tragic accident. Determined to provide strength and stability for her child, she chose to move forward and applied to join Dubai Police. Her acceptance marked a turning point that launched her military career.",
      "From trainee to trainer",
      "Thanks to her discipline and outstanding performance, Lieutenant Doha was selected as leader of a group of graduates. She later joined a trainers preparation course, where she was the only woman among the participants and achieved an excellent grade. This success led to her appointment as an official trainer at the Dubai Police Academy, reflecting the institution’s confidence in its national talent and its commitment to empowering promising professionals.",
      "Lieutenant Doha described one of her most emotional moments as seeing her son Younes take part in a graduation ceremony and recite the military oath under the direct guidance of the Commander-in-Chief, a memory she says will remain with her forever.",
